    <string name="guide">Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_skip">Skip</string>
    <string name="guide_next">Next</string>
    <string name="guide_start">Let\'s start!</string>
    <string name="guide_p0_title">Welcome to Cubetto</string>
    <string name="guide_p0_1">With Cubetto you make custom figures for the first-generation FABA™, with the songs you choose.</string>
    <string name="guide_p0_2">The path is always the same: songs → figure with an ID → copy to the box over USB → NFC tag under the figure.</string>
    <string name="guide_p0_3">You can open this guide again at any time with the ? button at the top of the Library and Box tabs.</string>
    <string name="guide_p1_title">1 · Create a figure</string>
    <string name="guide_p1_1">Tap “Create a new figure” and choose a name, colour and photo.</string>
    <string name="guide_p1_2">Pick an ID: it is the number the box reads from the tag and the name of the folder on the box. Suggested IDs don\'t clash with the original figures in your language.</string>
    <string name="guide_p1_3">Each figure can hold up to 99 songs.</string>
    <string name="guide_p2_title">2 · Add the songs</string>
    <string name="guide_p2_1">Paste a YouTube link in the Add tab, or use Share from the YouTube app. Playlists become several songs.</string>
    <string name="guide_p2_2">You can also pick files from the phone: MP3, M4A, OPUS, WAV or videos (only the audio is used).</string>
    <string name="guide_p2_3">Downloading and converting to the FABA™ format happen in the background, with a notification: you can even close the app.</string>
    <string name="guide_p2_4">In the figure you reorder songs by dragging them and listen to them with the player.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_title">3 · Copy to the box over USB</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_1">When connected to the phone, the first-generation FABA™ behaves like a USB stick: no computer or root needed. You only need a USB OTG cable or adapter.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_2">Turn on the FABA™ and plug it in. Android asks for permission to access the box: tick “always”, so next time Cubetto opens and copies by itself.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_3">Cubetto copies only the figures with changes, and only the changed songs of each. It first checks the free space and the 99-song limit.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_4">Before overwriting a folder on the box it backs it up on the phone: you can restore it from the Box tab. Automatic copying can be turned off in Settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3_5">Don\'t unplug the cable while copying. When it\'s done, tap Eject and unplug when the app says you can: like on a computer, so the box saves everything.</string>
    <string name="guide_p4_title">4 · Write the NFC tag</string>
    <string name="guide_p4_1">Open the figure, tap “Write tag” and hold a blank tag against the back of the phone until the app confirms. The tag is read back to check it.</string>
    <string name="guide_p4_2">Use genuine NXP NTAG213 or NTAG215 tags: many cheap clones are not read by the box. The same screen shows which ones to buy.</string>
    <string name="guide_p4_3">Glue the tag under a cardboard or 3D-printed base, put the figure on the FABA™ and enjoy!</string>
    <string name="guide_p4_4">With the NFC button at the top of the Library you read a figure, find out its ID and can copy it to a blank tag.</string>
    <string name="guide_p5_title">Before you start</string>
    <string name="guide_p5_1">Don\'t connect the box to the original FABA™ software: it could overwrite your songs.</string>
    <string name="guide_p5_2">Cubetto does not decrypt original figures: it only adds your own content, it doesn\'t replace them.</string>
    <string name="guide_p5_3">Only use content you have the right to download and listen to.</string>
    <string name="nfc_bring_tag">Bring the tag close</string>
    <string name="nfc_bring_figure">Bring the figure close</string>
    <string name="nfc_bring_hint">Place the disc on the back of the phone, near the camera, and hold it still for a second.</string>
    <string name="nfc_chip_auto_title">I detect the chip by myself</string>
    <string name="nfc_chip_auto_text">NTAG213 and NTAG215 are fine. If the chip is a clone the FABA™ can\'t read, I\'ll warn you before writing.</string>
